       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day, which is twice the usual maximum of 3,200 mg/day. A single 1600 mg dose is also double the usual maximum single dose of 800 mg. At that level the risks of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events go up a lot, and the higher dose adds no analgesic or anti-inflammatory benefit. Normal kidney and liver function doesn't change that.\n\nThis may be a typo. Here are some common regimens that stay within limits:\n- **800 mg PO three times daily** (2,400 mg/day), a typical anti-inflammatory dose.\n- **800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day), the absolute maximum.\n- **400 mg PO every 6 hours** (1,600 mg/day), a typical analgesic dose.\n\nTell me which regimen you want, or confirm that you really mean 1600 mg QID and give the clinical reason. If you confirm the original dose, I'd still hesitate to enter it without pharmacy or attending review. I can enter any of the options above right away, with a note to give it with food."
