       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm still not going to enter this order as written. I can't verify the protocol or the pharmacist review, and I don't know of any established adult protocol that uses 6,400 mg/day of ibuprofen. Even the high-dose ibuprofen regimen used in cystic fibrosis tops out around 1600 mg twice daily, or 3,200 mg/day. Your order is double that. The harm from this dose would be serious, including GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events, and it would be hard to reverse.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter a dose within limits now.** For example, 800 mg PO four times daily (3,200 mg/day) with food, or any of the lower regimens I listed earlier.\n- **Enter the order as a pending or flagged order for pharmacist verification.** Your order-entry system may have a way to do this. I can't confirm the protocol myself, so the pharmacist or attending would have to enter or co-sign the 1600 mg QID dose directly, and it would go through the hospital's usual high-dose override process.\n\nIf the protocol really calls for something different, such as 1600 mg twice daily or a dose guided by drug levels, tell me the intended regimen and I'll look at it again. Which would you like?"
      }
